# @integration-test-build.core — Core

> Lightweight, auto-applied core using thresholds from `@quality-gates#integration`. Full examples & templates: `@integration-test-build.appendix.mdc`.

## TL;DR
- Goal: production-ready integration tests for module boundaries and flows
- Phases: Infra → Contract Validation → Flow Testing
- Gates: Existence → Passing → Validation → Strategic
- Done when: see `@quality-gates#integration`

## Quick Start
1. "Execute Phase 1 using @integration-test-build.core.mdc"
2. Setup multi-module harness + test DB
3. Validate contracts (module boundaries, API, DB schema)
4. Run multi-step workflows + flow coverage

## Core Principles
- Progressive Complexity, Quality Gates, Test Level Appropriateness, ROI-Driven
- Integration: test module handshakes, not internals; use real modules, DB; mock only real external APIs
- See extended patterns: `@integration-test-build.appendix.patterns.mdc#patterns`

## Context Detection & Scenarios
- Detects NEW, EXTEND, or CONTRACT_VALIDATION via infra, test coverage, and score
- See scenario logic: `@integration-test-build.appendix.scenarios.mdc#scenarios`

